  "description": "AROXEK crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C42 H109 N7 O25 Yb4 8+,Cl4 Zn1 2-,H1 Cl3 O1 Zn1 2-,4(Cl1 1-),8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 1 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.641-3.803 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.40-109.04°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Yb4(μ3-OH)4(C6H13NO2)7(H2O)7][ZnCl4][ZnCl3(OH)]Cl4·8H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 7 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II), I(I), I(I).",
